    <summaries>
      <summary>
        <versionCode>00</versionCode>
        <actionDate>2025-12-17</actionDate>
        <actionDesc>Introduced in Senate</actionDesc>
        <updateDate>2026-10-15T15:52:21Z</updateDate>
        <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Federal Firearm Licensing Act</strong></p><p>This bill generally&nbsp;requires an individual to obtain a&nbsp;license before purchasing, receiving, or possessing a firearm. The bill also requires background checks for firearms transfers between private parties (i.e., unlicensed individuals).</p><p>Specifically, this bill requires individuals who purchase, receive, or possess a firearm to have a valid federal firearm purchasing license (or a state firearm purchasing license with substantially similar requirements). The bill requires the Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms and Explosives to establish a federal system for issuing firearm purchasing licenses and sets forth requirements for the system, including eligibility requirements for a license (e.g., training in firearms safety and background investigation and criminal history check), standards for denying or revoking a license, and requirements for reporting transactions.</p><p>The bill makes it unlawful to&nbsp;(1) purchase, receive, or possess a firearm without a valid firearm purchaser license; or (2) sell or transfer a firearm to an individual who does not have a valid firearm purchaser license or fail to report such a sale or&nbsp;transfer to law enforcement.</p><p>Additionally, the bill&nbsp;prohibits a firearm transfer between private parties unless a federal firearms licensee (e.g., gun dealer) first takes possession of the firearm to conduct a background check.</p>]]></text>
      </summary>
    </summaries>
